{
  "doc_id": "chapter_45_mika",
  "chapter": 45,
  "title": null,
  "when": null,
  "where": null,
  "scope": null,
  "entities": [],
  "scene_id": "chapter_45_mika",
  "segment_index": 0,
  "segment_count": 420,
  "segment_hash": "e6990f5c96cc",
  "block_title": "chapter_45_mika",
  "beats": [
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "CHAPTER 45: THE HOMECOMING"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 1: RETURN THROUGH SCORCH"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The desert remembered them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The Scorch breathed its dry, ancient breath over the column of four hundred and sixty souls as they marched eastward."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were a patchwork army—two hundred and ten Legion veterans moving with the stiff, automatic gait of soldiers who had marched to hell and back, and two hundred and fifty freed slaves, their steps uneven but fierce with new purpose."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The heat shimmered above the salt flats, distorting the memories of blood and battle into wavering ghosts."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt walked at the head, his Stage 1 wings folded tight against his back."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They caught the sun, casting a jagged, dragon-shaped shadow that stretched ahead of him like a guide."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika walked at his side, her eyes perpetually scanning the horizon, a habit war had etched into her bones."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They spoke little."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The silence between them was not empty; it was full of the unspoken understanding that the mission was over, and the weight of what came next was settling upon them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Weeks bled into one another, marked by the twin suns rising and setting over the endless ochre wastes."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They followed the Star Needle's faint resonance in Geralt's bones, a homing pulse pulling them toward the crash site, toward the place this had all begun."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then, one morning, they saw it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A smudge on the horizon resolved into walls."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Real, constructed walls of fitted stone, rising from the mountain's scar."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Smoke curled from chimneys."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The skeletal wreckage of the Anunnaki ship was still visible, but now it was integrated—girders repurposed as support beams, hull plating forming roofs."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Life had taken root in the wound."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Mika",
      "text": "\"Ironspire,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They approached slowly, a massive column emerging from the desert."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Sentries on the walls spotted them, and a cry went up—not of alarm, but of recognition."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The gates swung open."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly Sundrift met them just inside, her hands covered in brick-dust, her face older and wiser than when they'd last seen her at the collapsing Hub Needle."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Commander."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt.\" Her eyes took in the wings, the army of freed souls behind them, and a slow smile spread across her face."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"You did it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "You actually did it.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Geralt",
      "text": "\"We did,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly ushered them in, calling for water and food to be brought for the weary travelers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The town was a marvel of pragmatic beauty."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Stone houses with metal-reinforced doors."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A central well with a clever pulley system."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Workshops humming with activity."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Fields of hardy, genetically-modified crops growing in terraced plots against the mountain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was alive."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Mika",
      "text": "\"Where are the founders?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly's smile turned wry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Sleeping.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She led them to a sturdy longhouse near the center of town."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Inside, in a room filled with maps and building plans, two men were sprawled on cots."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Roric and Kael."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Deep in sleep, mouths slightly open, utterly dead to the world."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly walked over."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Roric?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Company.\" Nothing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She shook his shoulder."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Roric."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Wake up.\" A snore."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Finally, she kicked the leg of the cot."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"RORIC!"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "THE ARMY'S HERE!\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Roric snorted, rolled over, and continued sleeping."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Kael didn't even twitch."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly shrugged, turning back to Geralt and Mika."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"They do this."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Work themselves into the ground for days, then crash for twelve hours straight."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Sleep like the dead.\" She paused, a flicker of memory crossing her face."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Some things never change, huh?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika felt a strange, warm weight in her chest."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She remembered Zephyr's report, years ago now: They slept through a spaceship crash."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Here, in safety, they still slept through an army's homecoming."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Celly gave them a tour as the Legion and freed slaves integrated, some finding family among Ironspire's population, others simply collapsing in grateful exhaustion."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The settlement was more than just survival; it was a community."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A school was being planned."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A infirmary already running."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Celly",
      "text": "\"More survivors keep arriving,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She led them to the western edge of town, where the mountain scar deepened."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A team was there, carefully excavating something massive and metallic from the rock."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"We found this a few months back."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Been buried for... we don't know."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Millennia?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It's big."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Feels important."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Gives off a low hum.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt felt it immediately through his connection to Luminaire's Echo—a dormant network node, a piece of the ancient Void Spire infrastructure, sleeping beneath the earth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He exchanged a look with Mika."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Another anchor point."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They stayed for three days."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Some of the freed slaves chose to remain in Ironspire, their fight done, craving simple walls and steady work."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Some Legion veterans, too weary for another march, integrated into the town's guard."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The core group that gathered to move on was smaller, tighter: Geralt, Mika, Oreck, and about fifty of the most loyal, restless veterans."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They left at dawn, passing through Ironspire's gates and making the short trek to the nearby Star Needle Spire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It stood where Geralt had first returned from the Nexus, humming softly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "From there, they picked up an old, faint trail leading north and east, into the rocky foothills."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The path was familiar in Geralt's bones."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He had walked it alone, bleeding and desperate, years ago."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 2: THE FALCON RIDGE FOUNDING"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They reached the plateau by midday."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The air was thinner here, cooler."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The place was unremarkable—just a flat stretch of wind-scoured stone between two ridges—but both Geralt and Mika stopped as if struck."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika walked to a particular depression in the rock, her boots scuffing the stone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I fell here,\" she said, her voice quiet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I was following your blood."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "I thought it was leading me to you."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "I collapsed right here.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt moved a few meters to the east, to a patch of darker stone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I fell here first."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Before you ever came looking."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The Nexus spat me out."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "I crawled this far before I passed out.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They stood in silence, the space between them suddenly charged with the ghost of those terrible, lonely hours."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They had been meters apart, each unconscious, each believing the other was lost forever."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The distance felt vast and insignificant all at once."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then, a cry from above."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Three falcons circled against the hard blue sky."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They were the same ones—Mika knew it in her gut."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They wheeled once, twice, then dove sharply beyond the northern rise."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika and Geralt looked at each other."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "she",
      "text": "\"Again?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "he",
      "text": "\"Again,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They followed, their small company trailing behind."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They crested the rise—"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "—and the valley opened below them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was hidden, perfectly sheltered by the surrounding ridges."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A clear stream cut through its center, fed by a waterfall that cascaded from the eastern cliff."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Ancient, gnarled trees dotted the slopes, and the floor was rich, dark soil."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was a bowl of life carved into the stone desert."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Mika",
      "text": "\"The place we missed by fifty meters,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt pointed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "High on the cliff face, beneath the falcons' now-visible nest, a scrap of fabric fluttered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika scrambled up the loose scree, her heart pounding."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She pulled it free."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was the scarf."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her scarf."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The one she'd lost years ago on this very plateau, the one with the ambiguous, blood-stained pattern that could be a falcon or a dragon."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was sun-faded, but the stain was still there."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His blood."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her history."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"How is this here?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "she breathed."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No answer came."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The wind sighed through the valley."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Some rhymes in reality had no reason, only resonance."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt climbed up to join her."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He took the scarf from her trembling hands."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He found a straight, strong branch from a fallen tree."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "With careful, deliberate movements, he tied the scarf to one end."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He carried it down into the heart of the valley, to where the stream entered from the north."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He drove the branch deep into the earth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The makeshift banner caught the breeze, the faded fabric snapping once, then settling."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Geralt",
      "text": "\"Welcome to Falcon Ridge,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And they began to build."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 3: EARLY DAYS"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Month 1 was raw survival."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They cleared a flat space near the stream with axes and sheer will."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The first structure was a simple hut of stone and timber—Geralt and Mika's."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The second was a long barracks for the soldiers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It was basic, drafty, and home."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Month 2 brought order."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Merra Sundrift arrived from Ironspire with a caravan of seeds, tools, and stubborn hope."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She walked the south-facing slope with Mika, pointing where the sun would linger."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They planted the first fields."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt and the veterans channeled the stream, creating irrigation ditches with precise, military efficiency."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A storage cache was dug into a cool hillside."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Month 3 saw the valley become a settlement."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "More veterans arrived from Ironspire, their war ended, seeking the quiet company of their commanders."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Oreck took charge of construction, his methodical, powerful presence perfect for lifting stone beams and plotting defensive lines."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A low perimeter wall began to snake around the valley's most accessible approaches."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The valley's strategic perfection was undeniable."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It overlooked the only easy approach."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The Star Needle Spire was a clear silhouette on the western horizon, a constant and comforting landmark."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "They had a two-mile sightline—any approaching threat would be seen with hours of warning."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "One morning, as Mika inspected the growing wall, she turned and found Zephyr standing beside her, as if he'd been there for hours."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He was studying the masonry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Perimeter's good,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the ancient Sage said, not looking at her. \"Won't stop me, though.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Then he was gone, leaving only the scent of ozone and timelessness."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 4: THE FIRST TONGUE"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A year had gentled Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The fields were green."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The huts had become houses."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The archive was Mika's pride—a solid stone building with a vaulted ceiling, filled with empty shelves waiting for knowledge."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "One evening, Geralt, Mika, and Zephyr sat by the central fire."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The conversation drifted, as it often did with Zephyr, toward the deep past."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Zephyr",
      "text": "\"The First Tongue isn't spoken,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika leaned forward."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"The language of creation?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"One of them. The one this world was sung in.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He looked at her, his ancient eyes reflecting the fire. \"Would you like to hear a word?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She nodded."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Zephyr",
      "text": "\"Sek'han,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika looked at a fist-sized stone near her foot."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She focused, not on moving it with force, but on introducing the concept of sek'han to it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She didn't speak aloud."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She let the meaning form in her mind, in her will."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The stone lifted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Smoothly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Silently."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Three feet into the air, where it hung, turning slowly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika stared at it, then at her hand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "There had been no strain."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "No epic struggle."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "It had felt... obvious."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Like recalling a melody she'd forgotten she knew."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr was staring at her, his usual placidity replaced by sharp, assessing interest."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"That,\" he said slowly, \"should have taken months of meditation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Years, for most.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Mika",
      "text": "\"It felt natural,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "That night, by candlelight in the archive, Mika took out a blank ledger."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her hand did not shake."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I need to document this,\" she said to Geralt, who watched from the doorway."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Before I forget how easy it felt.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She titled the first page: On Resonance and Intent."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "And she began to write."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 5: TIME PASSING"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Year 2."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The archive grew, its shelves filling with Mika's precise handwriting."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The Needle Spire on the horizon began to glow with a soft, steady light at night."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Drawn by its energy, a new settlement sprang up at its base—the Sundrift family and other pioneers, building a community of engineers and mystics."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge remained smaller, a place of quiet study and green growth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Year 3."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr became a regular visitor, though never a resident."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He and Mika would spend hours in the archive, her writing, him offering corrections that felt less like instruction and more like reminders."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"The word for 'binding' has a secondary resonance for 'healing,' but only if your heart- tone is in the minor key,\" he'd say, and she would nod, scribbling in the margin."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt learned by osmosis, the concepts weaving into his understanding of the dragon armor's power."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Year 4."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "From the ridge, they could see Ironspire's expansion—new walls, watchtowers, the smoke of industry."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Trade caravans now moved regularly between the two settlements and the Sundrift Spire-town."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge supplied rare herbs and knowledge; Ironspire provided metalwork and grain; the Spire-town offered technical skill."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "A fragile, thriving network."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Year 5."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Oreck stood at the valley entrance at dawn, a pack on his back."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt and Mika came to see him off."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I'm not built for quiet,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the massive man said, his voice still layered with the faint hum of his Anunnaki augmentations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "Geralt",
      "text": "\"Where will you go?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Somewhere that needs defending. Somewhere that needs... action.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He looked at Mika. \"Thank you. For everything.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "she",
      "text": "\"You saved us as much as we saved you,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"We're even, then.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He turned and walked down the path, into the rising sun. He never returned. The valley felt quieter, more peaceful, and somehow less complete without his solid, restless presence."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 6: THE QUIET YEARS"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Year 6."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "An evening in late autumn."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The fire was low."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr was away on one of his endless walks."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The soldiers, now farmers and builders, had long since learned to give their commanders this evening silence."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Mika was sixty-three."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her hair was fully silver, her face lined with smiles and sorrows in equal measure."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She watched the embers die, her hand resting on the completed, massive tome in her lap—The First Tongue: A Primer for Those Who Would Speak Creation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "she",
      "text": "\"The book's done,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt sat beside her."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Time had not touched him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The scars that crisscrossed his skin were as stark as the day he’d earned them."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "His face, though hardened by millennia of memory, bore no new lines."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I know\" he said"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I'm done.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"I know.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The silence that followed was full and final."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The stars above Falcon Ridge were impossibly bright."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She went to bed first."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He kissed her forehead, the gesture worn smooth by decades of repetition."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "he",
      "text": "\"See you tomorrow,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "she",
      "text": "\"See you tomorrow,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She did not wake in the morning."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "ACT 7: AFTER"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Weeks later, Geralt walked through the bustling streets of Ironspire alone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He carried a large, cloth-wrapped package."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The town was noise and life—children shouting, blacksmiths hammering, the smell of baking bread."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "At the center of town stood the new library, a grand structure of stone and glass, Celly Sundrift's greatest project."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt entered the hushed interior."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Sunlight streamed through high windows onto a central pedestal of polished black stone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He approached, unwrapped the package, and placed the book upon it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "THE FIRST TONGUE: A PRIMER FOR THOSE WHO WOULD SPEAK CREATION"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "By Mika Covenant"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He opened it to the first page, where her dedication was written in a firm, elegant hand: For those who come after."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "May you build with kinder words."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He left it there, for the scholars, the seekers, the next generation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He walked back through the gates, nodding to guards who saluted him with deep respect."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "At the growing Sundrift settlement around the Needle Spire, he stopped at a market stall."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He bought a loaf of dark bread and, from a small garden plot, a bunch of late-blooming blueflowers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"For Mika,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "he told the gardener, a young woman with Merra's eyes."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "say",
      "who": "unknown",
      "text": "\"She'd like those,\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "the girl said softly."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He walked the now-familiar path up to Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He left the bread on the porch of their hut—one of the veterans would find it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He continued to the valley entrance, where the banner still flew."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The scarf was threadbare now, the bloodstain faded to a rust-colored whisper, the pattern forever ambiguous."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Beside it was a simple stone marker."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "MIKA COVENANT"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Commander."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Scholar."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Wife."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "She Followed Falcons Home."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He placed the blueflowers against the cool stone."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He sat beside the grave, his wings a dark mantle around him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He watched the valley—the stream she’d charted, the trees they’d planted together, the quiet industry of the home they’d built."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The mission was complete."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The life had been lived."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The love had been earned."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Through the bond, carried on Luminaire's distant, eternal Echo, a faint impression brushed his mind, clear and sure: She mattered."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt closed his eyes."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"I know.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "When he opened them, Zephyr was sitting beside him."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "He hadn't heard him approach."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "The Sage looked at the grave, then at the weathered book in the distance, then at Geralt."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"The teaching is preserved,\" he said."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"The knowledge is safe."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Her work is done.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Geralt looked at the setting sun, painting Falcon Ridge in amber and violet."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"What now?\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "Zephyr stood, extending a hand."
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "\"Now,\" he said, his voice holding the weight of coming eons, \"we prepare you.\""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "text": "END OF CHAPTER 45"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "line": 1,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "CHAPTER 45: THE HOMECOMING"
    },
    {
      "line": 2,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 3,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 1: RETURN THROUGH SCORCH"
    },
    {
      "line": 4,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 5,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The desert remembered them."
    },
    {
      "line": 6,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Scorch breathed its dry, ancient breath over the column of four hundred and sixty souls as they marched eastward."
    },
    {
      "line": 7,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were a patchwork army—two hundred and ten Legion veterans moving with the stiff, automatic gait of soldiers who had marched to hell and back, and two hundred and fifty freed slaves, their steps uneven but fierce with new purpose."
    },
    {
      "line": 8,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The heat shimmered above the salt flats, distorting the memories of blood and battle into wavering ghosts."
    },
    {
      "line": 9,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 10,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt walked at the head, his Stage 1 wings folded tight against his back."
    },
    {
      "line": 11,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They caught the sun, casting a jagged, dragon-shaped shadow that stretched ahead of him like a guide."
    },
    {
      "line": 12,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika walked at his side, her eyes perpetually scanning the horizon, a habit war had etched into her bones."
    },
    {
      "line": 13,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They spoke little."
    },
    {
      "line": 14,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The silence between them was not empty; it was full of the unspoken understanding that the mission was over, and the weight of what came next was settling upon them."
    },
    {
      "line": 15,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 16,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Weeks bled into one another, marked by the twin suns rising and setting over the endless ochre wastes."
    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They followed the Star Needle's faint resonance in Geralt's bones, a homing pulse pulling them toward the crash site, toward the place this had all begun."
    },
    {
      "line": 18,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 19,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then, one morning, they saw it."
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A smudge on the horizon resolved into walls."
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Real, constructed walls of fitted stone, rising from the mountain's scar."
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Smoke curled from chimneys."
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The skeletal wreckage of the Anunnaki ship was still visible, but now it was integrated—girders repurposed as support beams, hull plating forming roofs."
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Life had taken root in the wound."
    },
    {
      "line": 26,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Ironspire,\"",
      "speaker": "Mika",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Mika",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 28,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They approached slowly, a massive column emerging from the desert."
    },
    {
      "line": 30,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sentries on the walls spotted them, and a cry went up—not of alarm, but of recognition."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The gates swung open."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 33,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly Sundrift met them just inside, her hands covered in brick-dust, her face older and wiser than when they'd last seen her at the collapsing Hub Needle."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Commander."
    },
    {
      "line": 35,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt.\" Her eyes took in the wings, the army of freed souls behind them, and a slow smile spread across her face."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"You did it."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "You actually did it.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 39,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"We did,\"",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Geralt",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 41,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly ushered them in, calling for water and food to be brought for the weary travelers."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The town was a marvel of pragmatic beauty."
    },
    {
      "line": 43,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Stone houses with metal-reinforced doors."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A central well with a clever pulley system."
    },
    {
      "line": 45,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Workshops humming with activity."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Fields of hardy, genetically-modified crops growing in terraced plots against the mountain."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was alive."
    },
    {
      "line": 48,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Where are the founders?\"",
      "speaker": "Mika",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Mika",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 51,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly's smile turned wry."
    },
    {
      "line": 52,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Sleeping.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 53,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 54,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She led them to a sturdy longhouse near the center of town."
    },
    {
      "line": 55,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Inside, in a room filled with maps and building plans, two men were sprawled on cots."
    },
    {
      "line": 56,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Roric and Kael."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Deep in sleep, mouths slightly open, utterly dead to the world."
    },
    {
      "line": 58,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly walked over."
    },
    {
      "line": 60,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Roric?"
    },
    {
      "line": 61,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Company.\" Nothing."
    },
    {
      "line": 62,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She shook his shoulder."
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Roric."
    },
    {
      "line": 64,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wake up.\" A snore."
    },
    {
      "line": 65,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Finally, she kicked the leg of the cot."
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"RORIC!"
    },
    {
      "line": 67,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "THE ARMY'S HERE!\""
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 69,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Roric snorted, rolled over, and continued sleeping."
    },
    {
      "line": 70,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Kael didn't even twitch."
    },
    {
      "line": 71,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 72,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly shrugged, turning back to Geralt and Mika."
    },
    {
      "line": 73,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"They do this."
    },
    {
      "line": 74,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Work themselves into the ground for days, then crash for twelve hours straight."
    },
    {
      "line": 75,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sleep like the dead.\" She paused, a flicker of memory crossing her face."
    },
    {
      "line": 76,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Some things never change, huh?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 77,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 78,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika felt a strange, warm weight in her chest."
    },
    {
      "line": 79,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She remembered Zephyr's report, years ago now: They slept through a spaceship crash."
    },
    {
      "line": 80,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Here, in safety, they still slept through an army's homecoming."
    },
    {
      "line": 81,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 82,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Celly gave them a tour as the Legion and freed slaves integrated, some finding family among Ironspire's population, others simply collapsing in grateful exhaustion."
    },
    {
      "line": 83,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The settlement was more than just survival; it was a community."
    },
    {
      "line": 84,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A school was being planned."
    },
    {
      "line": 85,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A infirmary already running."
    },
    {
      "line": 86,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 87,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"More survivors keep arriving,\"",
      "speaker": "Celly",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Celly",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 88,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 89,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She led them to the western edge of town, where the mountain scar deepened."
    },
    {
      "line": 90,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A team was there, carefully excavating something massive and metallic from the rock."
    },
    {
      "line": 91,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"We found this a few months back."
    },
    {
      "line": 92,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Been buried for... we don't know."
    },
    {
      "line": 93,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Millennia?"
    },
    {
      "line": 94,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It's big."
    },
    {
      "line": 95,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Feels important."
    },
    {
      "line": 96,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Gives off a low hum.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 97,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt felt it immediately through his connection to Luminaire's Echo—a dormant network node, a piece of the ancient Void Spire infrastructure, sleeping beneath the earth."
    },
    {
      "line": 99,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He exchanged a look with Mika."
    },
    {
      "line": 100,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Another anchor point."
    },
    {
      "line": 101,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 102,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They stayed for three days."
    },
    {
      "line": 103,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Some of the freed slaves chose to remain in Ironspire, their fight done, craving simple walls and steady work."
    },
    {
      "line": 104,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Some Legion veterans, too weary for another march, integrated into the town's guard."
    },
    {
      "line": 105,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The core group that gathered to move on was smaller, tighter: Geralt, Mika, Oreck, and about fifty of the most loyal, restless veterans."
    },
    {
      "line": 106,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They left at dawn, passing through Ironspire's gates and making the short trek to the nearby Star Needle Spire."
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It stood where Geralt had first returned from the Nexus, humming softly."
    },
    {
      "line": 109,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "From there, they picked up an old, faint trail leading north and east, into the rocky foothills."
    },
    {
      "line": 110,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 111,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The path was familiar in Geralt's bones."
    },
    {
      "line": 112,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He had walked it alone, bleeding and desperate, years ago."
    },
    {
      "line": 113,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 114,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 2: THE FALCON RIDGE FOUNDING"
    },
    {
      "line": 115,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 116,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They reached the plateau by midday."
    },
    {
      "line": 117,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The air was thinner here, cooler."
    },
    {
      "line": 118,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The place was unremarkable—just a flat stretch of wind-scoured stone between two ridges—but both Geralt and Mika stopped as if struck.",
      "inferred": {
        "action": [
          {
            "label": "attack",
            "confidence": 0.9
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 119,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 120,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika walked to a particular depression in the rock, her boots scuffing the stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 121,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I fell here,\" she said, her voice quiet."
    },
    {
      "line": 122,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I was following your blood."
    },
    {
      "line": 123,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I thought it was leading me to you."
    },
    {
      "line": 124,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I collapsed right here.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 125,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 126,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt moved a few meters to the east, to a patch of darker stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 127,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I fell here first."
    },
    {
      "line": 128,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Before you ever came looking."
    },
    {
      "line": 129,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Nexus spat me out."
    },
    {
      "line": 130,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I crawled this far before I passed out.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 131,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 132,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They stood in silence, the space between them suddenly charged with the ghost of those terrible, lonely hours."
    },
    {
      "line": 133,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They had been meters apart, each unconscious, each believing the other was lost forever."
    },
    {
      "line": 134,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The distance felt vast and insignificant all at once."
    },
    {
      "line": 135,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 136,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then, a cry from above."
    },
    {
      "line": 137,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 138,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Three falcons circled against the hard blue sky."
    },
    {
      "line": 139,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They were the same ones—Mika knew it in her gut."
    },
    {
      "line": 140,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They wheeled once, twice, then dove sharply beyond the northern rise."
    },
    {
      "line": 141,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 142,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika and Geralt looked at each other."
    },
    {
      "line": 143,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 144,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Again?\"",
      "speaker": "she",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "she",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 145,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 146,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Again,\"",
      "speaker": "he",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "he",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 147,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 148,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They followed, their small company trailing behind."
    },
    {
      "line": 149,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They crested the rise—"
    },
    {
      "line": 150,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 151,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "—and the valley opened below them."
    },
    {
      "line": 152,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 153,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was hidden, perfectly sheltered by the surrounding ridges."
    },
    {
      "line": 154,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A clear stream cut through its center, fed by a waterfall that cascaded from the eastern cliff."
    },
    {
      "line": 155,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ancient, gnarled trees dotted the slopes, and the floor was rich, dark soil."
    },
    {
      "line": 156,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was a bowl of life carved into the stone desert."
    },
    {
      "line": 157,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 158,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"The place we missed by fifty meters,\"",
      "speaker": "Mika",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Mika",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 159,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 160,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt pointed."
    },
    {
      "line": 161,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "High on the cliff face, beneath the falcons' now-visible nest, a scrap of fabric fluttered."
    },
    {
      "line": 162,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika scrambled up the loose scree, her heart pounding."
    },
    {
      "line": 163,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She pulled it free."
    },
    {
      "line": 164,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 165,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was the scarf."
    },
    {
      "line": 166,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her scarf."
    },
    {
      "line": 167,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The one she'd lost years ago on this very plateau, the one with the ambiguous, blood-stained pattern that could be a falcon or a dragon."
    },
    {
      "line": 168,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was sun-faded, but the stain was still there."
    },
    {
      "line": 169,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His blood."
    },
    {
      "line": 170,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her history."
    },
    {
      "line": 171,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 172,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"How is this here?\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 173,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "she breathed."
    },
    {
      "line": 174,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 175,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No answer came."
    },
    {
      "line": 176,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The wind sighed through the valley."
    },
    {
      "line": 177,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Some rhymes in reality had no reason, only resonance."
    },
    {
      "line": 178,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 179,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt climbed up to join her."
    },
    {
      "line": 180,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He took the scarf from her trembling hands."
    },
    {
      "line": 181,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He found a straight, strong branch from a fallen tree."
    },
    {
      "line": 182,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "With careful, deliberate movements, he tied the scarf to one end."
    },
    {
      "line": 183,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He carried it down into the heart of the valley, to where the stream entered from the north."
    },
    {
      "line": 184,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He drove the branch deep into the earth."
    },
    {
      "line": 185,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 186,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The makeshift banner caught the breeze, the faded fabric snapping once, then settling."
    },
    {
      "line": 187,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 188,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Welcome to Falcon Ridge,\"",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Geralt",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 189,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 190,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And they began to build."
    },
    {
      "line": 191,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 192,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 3: EARLY DAYS"
    },
    {
      "line": 193,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 194,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Month 1 was raw survival."
    },
    {
      "line": 195,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They cleared a flat space near the stream with axes and sheer will."
    },
    {
      "line": 196,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The first structure was a simple hut of stone and timber—Geralt and Mika's."
    },
    {
      "line": 197,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The second was a long barracks for the soldiers."
    },
    {
      "line": 198,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It was basic, drafty, and home."
    },
    {
      "line": 199,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 200,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Month 2 brought order."
    },
    {
      "line": 201,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Merra Sundrift arrived from Ironspire with a caravan of seeds, tools, and stubborn hope."
    },
    {
      "line": 202,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She walked the south-facing slope with Mika, pointing where the sun would linger."
    },
    {
      "line": 203,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They planted the first fields."
    },
    {
      "line": 204,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt and the veterans channeled the stream, creating irrigation ditches with precise, military efficiency.",
      "inferred": {
        "action": [
          {
            "label": "creation",
            "confidence": 0.9
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 205,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A storage cache was dug into a cool hillside."
    },
    {
      "line": 206,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 207,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Month 3 saw the valley become a settlement."
    },
    {
      "line": 208,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "More veterans arrived from Ironspire, their war ended, seeking the quiet company of their commanders."
    },
    {
      "line": 209,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Oreck took charge of construction, his methodical, powerful presence perfect for lifting stone beams and plotting defensive lines."
    },
    {
      "line": 210,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A low perimeter wall began to snake around the valley's most accessible approaches."
    },
    {
      "line": 211,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 212,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The valley's strategic perfection was undeniable."
    },
    {
      "line": 213,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It overlooked the only easy approach."
    },
    {
      "line": 214,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Star Needle Spire was a clear silhouette on the western horizon, a constant and comforting landmark."
    },
    {
      "line": 215,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They had a two-mile sightline—any approaching threat would be seen with hours of warning."
    },
    {
      "line": 216,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 217,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One morning, as Mika inspected the growing wall, she turned and found Zephyr standing beside her, as if he'd been there for hours."
    },
    {
      "line": 218,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He was studying the masonry."
    },
    {
      "line": 219,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 220,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Perimeter's good,\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 221,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the ancient Sage said, not looking at her. \"Won't stop me, though.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 222,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 223,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then he was gone, leaving only the scent of ozone and timelessness."
    },
    {
      "line": 224,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 225,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 4: THE FIRST TONGUE"
    },
    {
      "line": 226,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 227,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A year had gentled Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "line": 228,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The fields were green."
    },
    {
      "line": 229,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The huts had become houses."
    },
    {
      "line": 230,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The archive was Mika's pride—a solid stone building with a vaulted ceiling, filled with empty shelves waiting for knowledge."
    },
    {
      "line": 231,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 232,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One evening, Geralt, Mika, and Zephyr sat by the central fire."
    },
    {
      "line": 233,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The conversation drifted, as it often did with Zephyr, toward the deep past."
    },
    {
      "line": 234,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 235,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"The First Tongue isn't spoken,\"",
      "speaker": "Zephyr",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Zephyr",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 236,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 237,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika leaned forward."
    },
    {
      "line": 238,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"The language of creation?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 239,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 240,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"One of them. The one this world was sung in.\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 241,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He looked at her, his ancient eyes reflecting the fire. \"Would you like to hear a word?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 242,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 243,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She nodded."
    },
    {
      "line": 244,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 245,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Sek'han,\"",
      "speaker": "Zephyr",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Zephyr",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 246,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 247,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika looked at a fist-sized stone near her foot."
    },
    {
      "line": 248,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She focused, not on moving it with force, but on introducing the concept of sek'han to it."
    },
    {
      "line": 249,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She didn't speak aloud."
    },
    {
      "line": 250,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She let the meaning form in her mind, in her will."
    },
    {
      "line": 251,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 252,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stone lifted."
    },
    {
      "line": 253,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Smoothly."
    },
    {
      "line": 254,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Silently."
    },
    {
      "line": 255,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Three feet into the air, where it hung, turning slowly."
    },
    {
      "line": 256,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 257,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika stared at it, then at her hand."
    },
    {
      "line": 258,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "There had been no strain."
    },
    {
      "line": 259,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "No epic struggle."
    },
    {
      "line": 260,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "It had felt... obvious."
    },
    {
      "line": 261,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Like recalling a melody she'd forgotten she knew."
    },
    {
      "line": 262,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 263,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr was staring at her, his usual placidity replaced by sharp, assessing interest."
    },
    {
      "line": 264,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"That,\" he said slowly, \"should have taken months of meditation."
    },
    {
      "line": 265,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Years, for most.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 266,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 267,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"It felt natural,\"",
      "speaker": "Mika",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Mika",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 268,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 269,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "That night, by candlelight in the archive, Mika took out a blank ledger."
    },
    {
      "line": 270,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her hand did not shake."
    },
    {
      "line": 271,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I need to document this,\" she said to Geralt, who watched from the doorway."
    },
    {
      "line": 272,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Before I forget how easy it felt.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 273,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 274,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She titled the first page: On Resonance and Intent."
    },
    {
      "line": 275,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And she began to write."
    },
    {
      "line": 276,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 277,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 5: TIME PASSING"
    },
    {
      "line": 278,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 279,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 2."
    },
    {
      "line": 280,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The archive grew, its shelves filling with Mika's precise handwriting."
    },
    {
      "line": 281,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Needle Spire on the horizon began to glow with a soft, steady light at night."
    },
    {
      "line": 282,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Drawn by its energy, a new settlement sprang up at its base—the Sundrift family and other pioneers, building a community of engineers and mystics."
    },
    {
      "line": 283,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge remained smaller, a place of quiet study and green growth."
    },
    {
      "line": 284,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 285,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 3."
    },
    {
      "line": 286,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr became a regular visitor, though never a resident."
    },
    {
      "line": 287,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He and Mika would spend hours in the archive, her writing, him offering corrections that felt less like instruction and more like reminders."
    },
    {
      "line": 288,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"The word for 'binding' has a secondary resonance for 'healing,' but only if your heart- tone is in the minor key,\" he'd say, and she would nod, scribbling in the margin."
    },
    {
      "line": 289,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt learned by osmosis, the concepts weaving into his understanding of the dragon armor's power."
    },
    {
      "line": 290,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 291,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 4."
    },
    {
      "line": 292,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "From the ridge, they could see Ironspire's expansion—new walls, watchtowers, the smoke of industry."
    },
    {
      "line": 293,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Trade caravans now moved regularly between the two settlements and the Sundrift Spire-town."
    },
    {
      "line": 294,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Falcon Ridge supplied rare herbs and knowledge; Ironspire provided metalwork and grain; the Spire-town offered technical skill."
    },
    {
      "line": 295,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "A fragile, thriving network."
    },
    {
      "line": 296,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 297,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 5."
    },
    {
      "line": 298,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Oreck stood at the valley entrance at dawn, a pack on his back."
    },
    {
      "line": 299,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt and Mika came to see him off."
    },
    {
      "line": 300,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 301,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"I'm not built for quiet,\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 302,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the massive man said, his voice still layered with the faint hum of his Anunnaki augmentations."
    },
    {
      "line": 303,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 304,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Where will you go?\"",
      "speaker": "Geralt",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "Geralt",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 305,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 306,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"Somewhere that needs defending. Somewhere that needs... action.\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 307,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He looked at Mika. \"Thank you. For everything.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 308,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 309,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"You saved us as much as we saved you,\"",
      "speaker": "she",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "she",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 310,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 311,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"We're even, then.\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 312,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He turned and walked down the path, into the rising sun. He never returned. The valley felt quieter, more peaceful, and somehow less complete without his solid, restless presence."
    },
    {
      "line": 313,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 314,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 6: THE QUIET YEARS"
    },
    {
      "line": 315,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 316,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 6."
    },
    {
      "line": 317,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "An evening in late autumn."
    },
    {
      "line": 318,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The fire was low."
    },
    {
      "line": 319,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr was away on one of his endless walks."
    },
    {
      "line": 320,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The soldiers, now farmers and builders, had long since learned to give their commanders this evening silence."
    },
    {
      "line": 321,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 322,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Mika was sixty-three."
    },
    {
      "line": 323,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her hair was fully silver, her face lined with smiles and sorrows in equal measure."
    },
    {
      "line": 324,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She watched the embers die, her hand resting on the completed, massive tome in her lap—The First Tongue: A Primer for Those Who Would Speak Creation."
    },
    {
      "line": 325,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 326,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"The book's done,\"",
      "speaker": "she",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "she",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 327,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 328,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt sat beside her."
    },
    {
      "line": 329,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Time had not touched him."
    },
    {
      "line": 330,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scars that crisscrossed his skin were as stark as the day he’d earned them."
    },
    {
      "line": 331,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "His face, though hardened by millennia of memory, bore no new lines."
    },
    {
      "line": 332,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I know\" he said"
    },
    {
      "line": 333,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 334,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"I'm done.\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 335,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 336,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"I know.\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 337,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 338,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The silence that followed was full and final."
    },
    {
      "line": 339,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stars above Falcon Ridge were impossibly bright."
    },
    {
      "line": 340,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 341,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She went to bed first."
    },
    {
      "line": 342,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He kissed her forehead, the gesture worn smooth by decades of repetition."
    },
    {
      "line": 343,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 344,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"See you tomorrow,\"",
      "speaker": "he",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "he",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 345,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 346,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"See you tomorrow,\"",
      "speaker": "she",
      "inferred": {
        "speaker_inferred": [
          {
            "value": "she",
            "confidence": 0.95
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "line": 347,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 348,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She did not wake in the morning."
    },
    {
      "line": 349,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 350,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "ACT 7: AFTER"
    },
    {
      "line": 351,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 352,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Weeks later, Geralt walked through the bustling streets of Ironspire alone."
    },
    {
      "line": 353,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He carried a large, cloth-wrapped package."
    },
    {
      "line": 354,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The town was noise and life—children shouting, blacksmiths hammering, the smell of baking bread."
    },
    {
      "line": 355,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "At the center of town stood the new library, a grand structure of stone and glass, Celly Sundrift's greatest project."
    },
    {
      "line": 356,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 357,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt entered the hushed interior."
    },
    {
      "line": 358,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sunlight streamed through high windows onto a central pedestal of polished black stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 359,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He approached, unwrapped the package, and placed the book upon it."
    },
    {
      "line": 360,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 361,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "THE FIRST TONGUE: A PRIMER FOR THOSE WHO WOULD SPEAK CREATION"
    },
    {
      "line": 362,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "By Mika Covenant"
    },
    {
      "line": 363,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 364,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He opened it to the first page, where her dedication was written in a firm, elegant hand: For those who come after."
    },
    {
      "line": 365,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "May you build with kinder words."
    },
    {
      "line": 366,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 367,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He left it there, for the scholars, the seekers, the next generation."
    },
    {
      "line": 368,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 369,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He walked back through the gates, nodding to guards who saluted him with deep respect."
    },
    {
      "line": 370,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "At the growing Sundrift settlement around the Needle Spire, he stopped at a market stall."
    },
    {
      "line": 371,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He bought a loaf of dark bread and, from a small garden plot, a bunch of late-blooming blueflowers."
    },
    {
      "line": 372,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 373,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"For Mika,\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 374,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "he told the gardener, a young woman with Merra's eyes."
    },
    {
      "line": 375,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 376,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "text": "\"She'd like those,\"",
      "speaker": "unknown"
    },
    {
      "line": 377,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "the girl said softly."
    },
    {
      "line": 378,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 379,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He walked the now-familiar path up to Falcon Ridge."
    },
    {
      "line": 380,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He left the bread on the porch of their hut—one of the veterans would find it."
    },
    {
      "line": 381,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He continued to the valley entrance, where the banner still flew."
    },
    {
      "line": 382,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The scarf was threadbare now, the bloodstain faded to a rust-colored whisper, the pattern forever ambiguous."
    },
    {
      "line": 383,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 384,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Beside it was a simple stone marker."
    },
    {
      "line": 385,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 386,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "MIKA COVENANT"
    },
    {
      "line": 387,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Commander."
    },
    {
      "line": 388,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Scholar."
    },
    {
      "line": 389,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Wife."
    },
    {
      "line": 390,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She Followed Falcons Home."
    },
    {
      "line": 391,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 392,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He placed the blueflowers against the cool stone."
    },
    {
      "line": 393,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He sat beside the grave, his wings a dark mantle around him."
    },
    {
      "line": 394,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He watched the valley—the stream she’d charted, the trees they’d planted together, the quiet industry of the home they’d built."
    },
    {
      "line": 395,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The mission was complete."
    },
    {
      "line": 396,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The life had been lived."
    },
    {
      "line": 397,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The love had been earned."
    },
    {
      "line": 398,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 399,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Through the bond, carried on Luminaire's distant, eternal Echo, a faint impression brushed his mind, clear and sure: She mattered."
    },
    {
      "line": 400,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 401,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt closed his eyes."
    },
    {
      "line": 402,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I know.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 403,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 404,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "When he opened them, Zephyr was sitting beside him."
    },
    {
      "line": 405,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "He hadn't heard him approach."
    },
    {
      "line": 406,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 407,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Sage looked at the grave, then at the weathered book in the distance, then at Geralt."
    },
    {
      "line": 408,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"The teaching is preserved,\" he said."
    },
    {
      "line": 409,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"The knowledge is safe."
    },
    {
      "line": 410,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Her work is done.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 411,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 412,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Geralt looked at the setting sun, painting Falcon Ridge in amber and violet."
    },
    {
      "line": 413,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"What now?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 414,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 415,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Zephyr stood, extending a hand."
    },
    {
      "line": 416,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Now,\" he said, his voice holding the weight of coming eons, \"we prepare you.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 417,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 418,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 419,
      "type": "blank"
    },
    {
      "line": 420,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "END OF CHAPTER 45"
    }
  ]
}